s to sustain that position through the finish. Markets and most raters treat the direction as settled, leaving the main uncertainty over the final margin rather than the winner.", "watch": "A late surge of Republican outside spending or an unusually tight governor's race at the top of the ticket could narrow Ossoff's lead in the final two weeks.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff seeks a second term against Representative Mike Collins, the Trump-endorsed Republican who secured his party's nomination through a runoff. Georgia sits only slightly to the right of the country overall, and every recent public poll shows Ossoff ahead, with margins ranging from four to twelve points. Surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters, including Trafalgar, Rasmussen, and Quantus, also show him leading, and polling averages place his advantage near eight to nine points.\n\nOssoff holds an enormous financial edge, having raised roughly $110 million to Collins' $10 million, and enters the final stretch with over $26 million on hand. Outside spending has been muted on both sides. Analysts mostly rate the contest Likely Democratic, with a few calling it Lean or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Ossoff's chances around 96 percent. The central question is the size of his margin, not the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9522, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9478, "margin"